From 3e0171503644ee71414893fa051029ee9b768a50 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josef Raschen <josef@raschen.org>
Date: Thu, 2 Jul 2026 09:38:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] net: phy: microchip_t1: report lan887x master/slave role
 before link-up

phydev->master_slave_get is only populated by read_status(), which does
not run before the PHY is started. Until then it reads
MASTER_SLAVE_CFG_UNSUPPORTED, so configuring the role of an interface
that is still administratively down, e.g. from an ifupdown pre-up hook
running "ethtool -s ... master-slave forced-slave", fails with
"master/slave configuration not supported by device".

Read the role back from the hardware at the end of config_init() so it
is known as soon as the PHY is initialized.

Fixes: 0941c8328234 ("net: phy: microchip_t1: Adds support for lan887x phy")
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 drivers/net/phy/microchip_t1.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/phy/microchip_t1.c b/drivers/net/phy/microchip_t1.c
index 8dc73175e989..8c4dcb01e341 100644
--- a/drivers/net/phy/microchip_t1.c
+++ b/drivers/net/phy/microchip_t1.c
@@ -1389,7 +1389,15 @@ static int lan887x_phy_init(struct phy_device *phydev)
 		return ret;
 
 	/* PHY interface setup */
-	return lan887x_config_phy_interface(phydev);
+	ret = lan887x_config_phy_interface(phydev);
+	if (ret < 0)
+		return ret;
+
+	/* Populate master_slave_get so that the master/slave role can be
+	 * changed through ethtool before the first link-up; otherwise
+	 * ethtool rejects the request as not supported by the device.
+	 */
+	return genphy_c45_pma_baset1_read_master_slave(phydev);
 }
 
 static int lan887x_100M_setup(struct phy_device *phydev)
